ting the thumbnail  okay so given all these capabilities you  want to start thinking about where could  we leverage cloud storage to solve  problems for our business one example  here is the Autism Speaks project  so what Autism Speaks wanted to do was  create a really large shared dataset  about genomic information related to  autism so every sequenced genome takes  up to 200 gigabytes of data they started  by sequencing roughly 1,300 genomes so  this created over a hundred terabytes of  data now 100 terabytes of data doesn't  seem that large but remember the car  it wasn't just these 1300 they wanted to  have 10,000 plus people who had their  genomes sequenced and now you're talking  multiple petabytes of data that's a  significant amount of data where can you  store this data so that you can control  who has access to it you can host it  relatively inexpensively and it has high  performance downloads around the world  well they did it on Google cloud  platform using GCS so they ended up  creating this data set that could be  used by the best scientists in the world  to run analyses against trillions of  data points to try to find new ways of  addressing autism in individuals you may  not have something quite this big or you  may have something actually bigger in  any case GCS probably will work really  well for you now after this session if  you come up with questions and you want  to learn more about cloud storage where  do you look search is your friend if you  search on Google Cloud storage and then  whatever topic you're interested in it's  very likely that the first link is going  to be what you want so for example here  we've searched on Google Cloud Storage  classes and what we get is a link to the  article that has all the information  that fed the table that we looked at  earlier if you're trying to figure out  the right command line structure for  doing things using the Jewess GS util  utility type in gsutil and then the  action that you want to perform