  recruiting your team and agreeing on  what you're testing a second segment  which is figuring out how you're going  to test this is generally some point  testing and some trial and error and  some research and then ultimately you  perform your tests you collect your data  and you analyze the results and you make  a decision if you put more people  against this you can get more use cases  test it out in the same time line if  it's a really sophisticated solution it  may take you a little bit longer but  hopefully this gives you a sense of how  to tackle the evaluation of GCS as an  appropriate technology for your use  cases and that's it for this session  thanks so much for joining us I hope you  learn something and that you enjoyed it  we'll be sending you a follow-up email  that has a link to a code lab where you  can get your hands dirty and try GCSE  out for yourself  we'd love your feedback so make sure to  provide that on screen and stay tuned  for our next session
 

